@startuml direct-rialto-lifecycle-error-sequence
title Error handling: Rialto FAILURE, playback errors and AAMP retune

participant "Rialto event\nthread" as EV
participant "AampRialtoPlayer" as P
participant "PlayerStateMachine" as SM
participant "Notifiable\n(AAMP scheduler)" as N
participant "AAMP core" as A
participant "AAMP control\nthread" as CT

== Fatal: PlaybackState FAILURE ==
EV -> P : OnPlaybackState(FAILURE)
P -> P : HandlePlaybackFailure()
P -> SM : onError()
note right of SM : any active state, including\nFLUSHING, -> ERROR;\nwakes a flush waiter
alt previous state not IDLE and not ERROR
  P -> N : NotifyPlaybackError(\nAAMP_TUNE_GST_PIPELINE_ERROR,\nretry=true)
  N -> A : SendErrorEvent (async task)
else stale (IDLE) or already reported (ERROR)
  P -> P : log only
end
note over P : In ERROR: PLAYING, PAUSED and SEEK_DONE are ignored.\nThe Flushing hold, if any, stays until Stop() resets it.

== Non-fatal: notifyPlaybackError ==
EV -> P : OnPlaybackError(sourceId, error)
P -> N : mapped notification\n(no state change)

== Recovery is AAMP's decision ==
A -> CT : retry / ScheduleRetune
CT -> P : Stop()
P -> SM : onStop(): ERROR -> IDLE
CT -> P : Configure() ... Stream()
note right of P : full rebuild; see the\nstartup sequence
@enduml
